<title>UK: Weekly Baltic, Black Sea oil exports post fresh fall.</title>
<headline>Weekly Baltic, Black Sea oil exports post fresh fall.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of crude oil and refined oil products from Baltic and Black Sea terminals in the fourth week of May fell 105,000 barrels per day (bpd) on the week to 1.767 million, Petro-Logistics said.</p>
<p>Exports from former-Soviet ports plus Romania and Bulgaria slipped back to those seen at the end of April, coming down from a recent high of 2.128 million bpd in the first week of May, the Geneva-based consultancy said.</p>
<p>Export levels remained 97,000 bpd above levels seen in the week of last year.</p>
<p>Crude exports, at 1.01 million bpd in the fourth week of May were down 111,000 bpd on the week. Fuel oil and gas oil also slipped slightly but gasoline and jet exports were higher.</p>
<p>The following table from Petro Logistics is a breakdown of petroleum exports from the Baltics and the Black Sea in the fourth week of May.</p>
<p>		 Crude oil    Fuel Oil   Gasoil   Mogas/Jet  Total</p>
<p>Total FSU	970,040    416,642    299,751   38,630  1,725,063</p>
<p>Rom/Bul					  5,427		   5,427</p>
<p>Total tonnes   970,040    416,642    305,178   38,630  1,730,490</p>
<p>Total bpd    1,010,227    385,394    324,579   46,417  1,766,617</p>
<p>Change on wk  -111,135    -18,415    -16,116  +40,768   -104,898</p>
<p>Change on yr  +116,497    +54,436    -84,828  +35,117    +96,644</p>
<p>Note: Naphtha exports were zero, down from 24,578 bpd last year.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom, +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
